  "result": {
    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: Jupyter Widgets\ndescription: Validating ipywidgets interactivity through the Quarto-to-Quartz bridge.\naliases:\n  - Jupyter Widgets\n  - ipywidgets\ntags:\n  - research/computation\n  - research/interactive\npublish: true\nformat: html\nexecute:\n  freeze: true\n  cache: true\n---\n\nJupyter Widgets let a Python author place JavaScript components on the page. There is no\nPython kernel behind a published site, so only the JavaScript half survives — the widget\nrenders and responds to the reader, but it cannot call back into Python. This note checks\nthat the surviving half arrives intact through the bridge described in\n[[Monte Carlo Simulation]].\n\n## Widget state without a kernel\n\nThe reliable pattern is `jslink`, which wires two widgets together entirely in the browser.\nDragging the slider below must move the progress bar and update the number, with no server\ninvolved.\n\n::: {#cell-linked-widgets .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport ipywidgets as widgets\n\nslider = widgets.IntSlider(\n    value=40, min=0, max=100, step=1, description=\"samples:\", continuous_update=True\n)\nprogress = widgets.IntProgress(value=40, min=0, max=100, description=\"coverage:\")\nreadout = widgets.IntText(value=40, description=\"value:\")\n\nwidgets.jslink((slider, \"value\"), (progress, \"value\"))\nwidgets.jslink((slider, \"value\"), (readout, \"value\"))\n\nwidgets.VBox([slider, progress, readout])\n```\n\n::: {#linked-widgets .cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```{=html}\n<script type=\"application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json\">\n{\"model_id\":\"99139459609341fab0d41edfb0251ecc\",\"version_major\":2,\"version_minor\":0,\"quarto_mimetype\":\"application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json\"}\n</script>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## A container widget\n\nTabs exercise the widget manager's layout handling rather than a single leaf control.\n\n::: {#cell-tabbed-widgets .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ntabs = widgets.Tab(\n    children=[\n        widgets.HTML(\"<p>Estimates converge at a rate of <code>n^-1/2</code>.</p>\"),\n        widgets.HTML(\"<p>Correlated draws inflate the effective error.</p>\"),\n    ]\n)\ntabs.set_title(0, \"Independent\")\ntabs.set_title(1, \"Correlated\")\ntabs\n```\n\n::: {#tabbed-widgets .cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<script type=\"application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json\">\n{\"model_id\":\"43fa8a479f0849cc9f7374f3e069892e\",\"version_major\":2,\"version_minor\":0,\"quarto_mimetype\":\"application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json\"}\n</script>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## A third-party widget\n\n`ipyleaflet` is a separate widget package with its own JavaScript bundle. It checks that the\nwidget manager resolves modules beyond the built-in `@jupyter-widgets/controls` set. The map\nshould pan and zoom.\n\n::: {#cell-leaflet-map .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfrom ipyleaflet import Map, Marker\n\nsite_map = Map(center=(51.5074, -0.1278), zoom=9)\nsite_map.add(Marker(location=(51.5074, -0.1278)))\nsite_map\n```\n\n::: {#leaflet-map .cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<script type=\"application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json\">\n{\"model_id\":\"1abff4f761414aca829220b24c5ebe06\",\"version_major\":2,\"version_minor\":0,\"quarto_mimetype\":\"application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json\"}\n</script>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nCompare with the Observable approach in [[Observable JS]].\n\n",
